      "observed": "The STM32L476 MCU U3 has its VBAT pin left unconnected: the netlist contains an explicit unconnected net for U3 pin 1, and U3 pin 1 is not present on the VCC net.",
      "expected": "For an STM32L476 with no backup battery, standard practice and the part's power-pin metadata require VBAT to be connected to VDD/VCC so the backup domain is powered; leaving a power_in pin floating is not a valid power connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"66\") (name \"unconnected-(U3-VBAT-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"VCC\") ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "The schematic does not show where VCC is generated; it is only consumed."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU backup domain may be unpowered or floating, which can affect RTC/backup-register behavior and may violate the MCU's power requirements even if the main core still boots.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity otherwise matches the specified NFC, OLED, touch, and SWD architecture, but the MCU VBAT power pin is explicitly left unconnected, which is a likely power-design anomaly for an STM32L476 without a backup battery."
}

